WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.560
This is Every Country in the World Part 2
By Wendover Productions.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:07.399
If you haven’t seen part 1, click here to
watch that first.

00:00:07.399 --> 00:00:10.710
We left off last time in Suriname, our 98th
country.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.870
Suriname is the only county other than the
Netherlands whose sole primary language is

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:18.210
Dutch, although there are other countries
that speak a creole version of Dutch like

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:22.689
Namibia which speaks Afrikaans which is just
close enough to Dutch that a Dutch and Namibian

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.060
could hold a conversation.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.009
Namibia has this long protrusion which gives
them access to the Zambezi river although

00:00:28.009 --> 00:00:32.200
they miss out by about 300 feet on bordering
Zimbabwe which is the country ferries have

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.080
the pass through when making the 600 foot
trip from Botswana to Zambia.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.760
This is likely the shortest ferry in the world
to cross through three countries.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:45.080
To the northeast of Zambia is one of the world’s
176 tripoints—triple border crossings.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.240
This one links Zambia to Malawi and Tanzania
whose northern border is a very straight line

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.410
across Lake Victoria which creates these two
tiny

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:52.770
cut off peninsulas.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:56.280
Uganda is a surprisingly progressive nation
with the highest representation of

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.420
women in parliament in the world at 63%.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.400
They also became the first country in the
world to

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.489
outright ban plastic bags in 2007.

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:07.190
The Solomon islands, on the other hand, only
has one woman

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:10.150
in their parliament or 2% representation.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:14.300
The Solomon Islands is home to the West Georgia
islands which share a name with Georgia which

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.470
kinda shares a name with Georges Plain in
Jamaica which is one of two countries in the

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:20.490
world whose flag doesn't share colors with
the

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:23.780
American flag—as in, no red, white, or blue.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:27.300
The other one is Mauritania, but Libya used
to be on that list until they changed their

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.990
flag from this to this in 2011.

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:33.030
Libya is so
large that its northwest point is closer to

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.159
to Luxembourg than to its southeast point.

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:37.830
Luxembourg
has the second highest per capita income in

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:40.549
the world behind Qatar—a small but mighty
country

00:01:40.549 --> 00:01:44.880
thats just a bit larger than Lebanon who shares
a southern border with the United Nations

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.100
Disengagement Observer Force Zone which is
an area essentially without sovereignty meant

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.060
to
serve as a buffer between Israeli controlled

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.909
Syria and Syria.

00:01:52.909 --> 00:01:56.729
One could call it… a de-militarized
zone, although the most famous DMZ is north

00:01:56.729 --> 00:02:00.590
of South Korea where, if you dig a hole straight
down and through the earth, you’d pop up

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:02.500
just off the coast of Uruguay.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.830
Uruguay was a military
dictatorship up until 1985 but Thailand still

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:08.259
is—the only current one.

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:12.440
Bangkok, Thailand is the
most visited city in the world at 16 million

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.480
yearly visitors which is a ton, especially
compared to

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:19.900
Vilnius, Lithuania which only sees 180,000
visitors per year.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:22.720
Lithuania has a rather straight
border though this lake which leads to two

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.620
peninsulas with their tops chopped off and
an

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:28.410
internationally divided island with Belarus
which has a rather straight border in this

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.720
lake which
leads to another peninsula with its top chopped

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.910
off and an internationally divided island
with

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:33.910
Latvia.

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:37.950
Latvia’s independence day is May the 4th
aka Star Wars day whose scenes on Tatooine

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.800
were filmed in Tunisia.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.069
Tunisia’s currency is the Dinar, which is
also the name for the currency

00:02:43.069 --> 00:02:44.290
in Macedonia.

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:47.750
If you look at Macedonia on a map, it will
almost always have FYROM under its

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:51.080
name which stands for Former Yugoslav Republic
of Macedonia.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:54.080
When Macedonia became an
independent country it picked this name but

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.850
Greece wasn’t all too happy about that since
their

00:02:55.850 --> 00:03:00.100
northern region is also called Macedonia so
the solution was to call the country the Former

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:04.879
Yugoslav Republic of Macedonia in all official
capacities, while colloquially its still known

00:03:04.879 --> 00:03:06.350
as
Macedonia.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:10.190
Greece is known for having a huge expatriated
population around the world and the

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:14.440
39th largest greek population in the world
is in Oman in the middle east.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:17.550
Inside Oman is an
exclave of the United Arab Emirates except

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.300
this part of Oman is actually an enclave inside
the

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:24.170
UAE which makes this the only double enclave
in the middle east.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:27.360
The UAE is one of 18
countries worldwide to not have a river—one

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:32.020
of which is Tonga which actually has an olympic
medal from their super heavyweight boxer—Paea

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.020
Wolfgramm.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.129
Another country that has one
total medal is Gabon whose southern border

00:03:36.129 --> 00:03:38.180
is shared with Congo whose southern border
is

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:40.830
shared with this rather large exclave of Angola.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:45.010
Only because of that exclave, Angola borders
both Congo and the Democratic Republic of

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:46.010
the Congo.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:48.710
These are of course two different
countries although they’re both named for

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:51.129
the Congo River—the deepest river in the
world at

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:54.180
more than 750 feet deep.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:57.010
Interestingly, despite being both enormous
countries, their current

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:00.250
capitals are just on opposite sides of the
Congo from each other.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:04.190
The DRC has this great clean
border with Rwanda which causes no problems

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:06.490
at all unlike this one in Austria.

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:09.239
Jungholz is only
connected to the rest of Austria by about

00:04:09.239 --> 00:04:11.980
15 feet of territory and no roads.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:15.610
Vienna, Austria used to
be the capital of the Austria-Hungarian empire

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:19.470
whose territory included present-day Italy,
Poland, Germany, Croatia, Montenegro, Serbia,

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.930
(all of which we’ve already talked about)
and

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:26.260
Bosnia and Herzegovina, the Czech Republic,
Hungary, Romania, Slovakia, and Ukraine.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:30.870
Ukraine has this southern section which isn’t
part of Russia yet, although its only connected

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.370
to
the rest of Ukraine by two roads, one of which

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:35.840
rather inconveniently passes through Moldova
for

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:37.560
only about 3 miles.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:41.310
Moldova is rated the third least touristy
country in the world since only one

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:47.270
tourist visits each year for every 323 citizens
although Bangladesh is the number one least

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:53.910
touristy country since for each yearly tourist
visit there are 1273 Bangladeshi citizens.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:57.139
Bahrain,
on the other hand, receives 7.7 tourist visits

00:04:57.139 --> 00:05:01.480
per citizen per year and also has an internationally
divided island, but this one was actually

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.750
very purposefully created to serve as the
passport

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:07.860
control point between Bahrain and Saudi Arabia
on the King Fahd Causeway.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:10.800
Saudi Arabia is
home to Mecca, the birthplace of the central

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.260
figure of Islam—the prophet Muhammad.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.669
Mecca
has a population of about 1.5 million people

00:05:15.669 --> 00:05:17.980
but during the Hajj—the yearly pilgrimage
to Mecca

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:21.580
—this triples to almost 5 million people.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:23.830
Land in Mecca is some of the most expensive
in the

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:26.930
world at up to $13,000 per square foot.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.170
Saudi Arabia really isn’t great friends
with their southern

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:34.380
neighbor—Yemem, who owns over 200 islands
including Socotra Island which is surprisingly

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:38.660
green compared to its mainland neighbors and
is the only place in the world where you can

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:40.490
find
the Dragons Blood Tree.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:43.860
Yemen’s national soccer team has played
Bhutan three times in the past

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:46.780
few decades all of which Bhutan lost rather
horribly.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:50.470
Bhutan is home to the Gangkhar Puensum
mountain which is believed to be the tallest

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:55.210
un-summited mountain in the world since local
spiritual beliefs prohibit anyone from climbing

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:57.590
a mountain over 6000 m (19500 feet).

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.479
This
mountain is in the himalayas range which if

00:05:59.479 --> 00:06:02.070
you follow to the west brings you to Nepal
which if

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:05.460
of course home to Mount Everest—the tallest
mountain in the world.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:11.310
Everest is 29,029 feet tall
—880 times higher than the Marshall Islands’

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:13.150
tallest peak at 33 feet.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:15.789
If you dig a hole straight
down through the earth from the Marshall Islands

00:06:15.789 --> 00:06:18.199
you arrive just off the coast of Liberia which
is

00:06:18.199 --> 00:06:21.610
the country of registration of 11% of the
world’s ships.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:29.110
Of the 2,771 registered ships, though,
only 190 are actually owned by Liberians.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:30.850
Foreigners register their ships there since
there are

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:33.229
few regulations and low costs.

00:06:33.229 --> 00:06:38.560
Malta also registers many ships for the same
reasons with 1,437

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:39.560
foreign owned ships.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:42.479
Malta is a European Union member which means
that we've almost talked

00:06:42.479 --> 00:06:44.340
about every EU member.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.930
Our last two are Estonia and Ireland whose
northernmost point is

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:50.740
actually farther north than Northern Ireland’s.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:53.220
Ireland has played Samoa six times in Rugby,
and

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:58.270
Samoa actually won once which is quite impressive
for a country of less than 200,000.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:01.900
Samoa’s
rugby team did once lose to New Zealand 101-14

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.850
though—they’re not that good.

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:06.480
New Zealand
has a kinda territory of Niue.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:09.780
It's recognized as a freely associated state--meaning
by choice—but

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:13.330
Niue isn't recognized by the UN as a independent
country.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:17.650
However, Niue is exactly on the
opposite side of the world from Niger which

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:19.130
is named for the Niger River.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:22.190
The Niger River has
probably the most bizarre river course in

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:24.840
the world—it starts only 150 miles from
the Atlantic

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:29.060
ocean but then takes a 2,600 mile path to
reach the ocean.

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:34.950
It starts in Sierra Leone, flows through
Guinea, Mali, Niger itself, then Benin before

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:36.789
reaching the ocean in Nigeria.

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:40.270
Nigeria is also
named after the Niger river and is by far

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:43.949
the most populous country in Africa at 125
million

00:07:43.949 --> 00:07:44.949
people.

00:07:44.949 --> 00:07:48.849
The least populous country in Africa is the
Seychelles which isn’t on the mainland but

00:07:48.849 --> 00:07:50.860
still considered an African country.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:54.639
They also have what might be the coolest flag
in the world

00:07:54.639 --> 00:07:58.819
except for maybe Saint Lucia's, but I have
to give a solid runners up position to Saint

00:07:58.819 --> 00:08:00.380
Vincent
and the Grenadines.

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:03.360
Saint Vincent and the Grenadines name is rather
purposefully similar to that

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:05.000
of its neighboring island—Grenada.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:08.750
Grenada’s airport wasn't built until 1985
but nowadays you

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:12.030
can fly to places like Port of Spain in Trinidad
and Tobago.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:16.069
Trinidad is also the name of
municipality of 20,000 people in Honduras

00:08:16.069 --> 00:08:20.940
which has two capitals—Tegucigalpa and
Comayagüela—much like the Cote d’Ivoire

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:23.750
whose capitals are are Yamoussoukro and Abidjan.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:28.599
Despite having a very easy English translation—the
Ivory coast—the Cote d’Ivoire is almost

00:08:28.599 --> 00:08:33.069
always referred to by this name since its
government refuses to accept any translated

00:08:33.069 --> 00:08:34.069
name.

00:08:34.069 --> 00:08:35.279
If
you draw a straight line south from Cote d’Ivoire

00:08:35.279 --> 00:08:37.539
until it crosses Antartica and goes North
you’ll

00:08:37.539 --> 00:08:41.899
end up intersecting Vanuatu which is one of
seven countries worldwide to not be part of

00:08:41.899 --> 00:08:44.069
the
International Criminal Police Organization

00:08:44.069 --> 00:08:46.129
also known as INTERPOL.

00:08:46.129 --> 00:08:48.619
Another non-
INTERPOL-member country is Tuvalu which is

00:08:48.619 --> 00:08:50.459
the second smallest country in the world to
have

00:08:50.459 --> 00:08:52.490
a commercial international airport.

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:55.290
This is also the second video in a row that
I’ve used this

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:58.179
image—watch my last video to find out why.

00:08:58.179 --> 00:09:00.480
Nauru is the smallest country outright to
have an

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.550
airport and it rather controversially has
camps for those who attempt to seek asylum

00:09:04.550 --> 00:09:07.369
in Australia,
many of whom are from Iraq.

00:09:07.369 --> 00:09:10.310
Iraq borders Iran, which has 22 ski resorts.

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:13.649
That’s more then the
entire South American continent.

00:09:13.649 --> 00:09:15.819
Speaking of South America, we haven’t covered
Paraguay

00:09:15.819 --> 00:09:20.040
which is another one of these landlocked countries
with a navy and with that, we’ve touched

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.060
on
every South American country!

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:24.100
If you dig a hole through the earth from Paraguay
and you end

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:28.420
up just north of Philippines which is our
seventh to last Asian country.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:30.949
The other ones are
Myanmar which is one of the worlds three countries

00:09:30.949 --> 00:09:35.619
not using the metric system; Timor-Leste
whose currency is the US dollar despite having

00:09:35.619 --> 00:09:38.429
no real connection to the US; Pakistan which
is

00:09:38.429 --> 00:09:42.399
home to the third-largest non-polar glacier
in the world despite being at the same latitude

00:09:42.399 --> 00:09:44.949
of
South Texas; Jordan which you might think

00:09:44.949 --> 00:09:47.019
is landlocked from looking at a map but actually
has

00:09:47.019 --> 00:09:52.180
a 16 mile coast on the red sea; Syria which
is home to Damascus—the oldest continuously

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:57.100
inhabited city on the planet; and Kuwait which
has the highest value currency in the world

00:09:57.100 --> 00:10:00.100
at 3.3
US dollars to each Kuwaiti Dinar.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:03.410
With that, we've covered every Asian country.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:06.190
One of the
lowest value currencies in the world is the

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:09.540
Sao Tomé and Principe dobra at 23,000 dobra
to the

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:10.540
dollar.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:13.950
Sao Tomé and Principe speaks Portuguese which
means we've covered every Portuguese

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:15.009
speaking country.

00:10:15.009 --> 00:10:18.459
The country is also off the coast of Cameroon
which became the first African

00:10:18.459 --> 00:10:23.100
country to reach the FIFA world cup semi-finals
in 1990, although that's since been

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:27.489
accomplished by Ghana where the official and
primary language is English and there are

00:10:27.489 --> 00:10:30.189
only
three more countries like this—Belize, the

00:10:30.189 --> 00:10:34.739
only English speaking country in central america;
Barbados, who has the third highest human

00:10:34.739 --> 00:10:40.579
development index score in the western hemisphere;
and Antigua and Barbuda whose native language—Taino—is

00:10:40.579 --> 00:10:45.049
the origin of english words like
Canoe, Barbecue, Hammock, and Hurricane.

00:10:45.049 --> 00:10:47.239
So we’ve covered every English speaking
country

00:10:47.239 --> 00:10:51.089
but there are two remaining countries that
were part of the British empire—Dominica,

00:10:51.089 --> 00:10:53.459
where
Antillean Creole is the primary language;

00:10:53.459 --> 00:10:55.829
and Mauritius which has the highest population
density

00:10:55.829 --> 00:10:59.149
in Africa at over 1500 per sq/mi.

00:10:59.149 --> 00:11:01.839
One of the lowest population densities in
Africa is in Central

00:11:01.839 --> 00:11:04.540
African Republic at 18 people per sq/mi.

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:07.100
The Central African Republic’s northern
neighbor is

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:12.410
Chad whose embassy in Washington DC is only
about 200 feet away from that of Burkina Faso

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:16.819
whose capital has perhaps the best name in
the world—Ougadougou.

00:11:16.819 --> 00:11:20.230
In the southeast of Burkina
Faso is this piece of Togo that is only connected

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:23.249
to the main part by a 300 foot wide strip
of land.

00:11:23.249 --> 00:11:27.589
This area’s roads, however, all come from
Burkina Faso which means that, much like Point

00:11:27.589 --> 00:11:32.309
Roberts, residents need to cross two international
borders to get to their own country.

00:11:32.309 --> 00:11:35.470
There are
only three African countries left—Comoros,

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:37.769
the second largest vanilla producer in the
world;

00:11:37.769 --> 00:11:41.489
Burundi, the poorest country in the world
to have an olympic medal; and Eritrea, which

00:11:41.489 --> 00:11:44.709
has
neither an official or majority spoken language.

00:11:44.709 --> 00:11:46.579
Drawing a latitude line west from Eritrea
brings

00:11:46.579 --> 00:11:50.029
you to Nicaragua—home to a lake on an island
in a lake.

00:11:50.029 --> 00:11:54.690
More than 100,000 nicaraguans live in
nearby El Salvador which is the smallest central

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:57.109
American country and only one to not have
a

00:11:57.109 --> 00:11:58.109
Caribbean coastline.

00:11:58.109 --> 00:12:00.940
El Salvador’s northern neighbor is Guatemala
whose border with Mexico

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:05.059
was originally defined by the course of the
Chixoy river but erosion has changed the course

00:12:05.059 --> 00:12:08.829
which created a bunch of enclaves and exclaves
like this, this, and this.

00:12:08.829 --> 00:12:10.959
And that’s our last
country in the western hemisphere!

00:12:10.959 --> 00:12:12.360
We're getting close!

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:15.749
Guatemala's embassy in Ottawa is about
900 feet away from Slovenia's which has this

00:12:15.749 --> 00:12:18.249
really messed up border with Croatia including
this

00:12:18.249 --> 00:12:22.869
tiny section that isn't actually claimed by
either country making it terra nullis.

00:12:22.869 --> 00:12:26.959
The 10th and final
country to end in -nia and our final country

00:12:26.959 --> 00:12:30.220
is Albania whose capital is one of the only
in Europe

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:31.610
to not have a McDonalds.

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:34.710
But wait, if you draw a latitude line from
the south of Albania that

